WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.900
A barchan moves downwind and its crescent tips point with the

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:04.640
wind.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.640
A parabolic dune has arms anchored by vegetation, so the tips

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.040
point upwind.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.200
Sand supply and changes in wind direction help explain the

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.940
other shapes on the slide.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.310
Wind carries sand up the gentle slope.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.010
Sand spills over the crest and avalanches down the steep

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.430
downwind face.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.270
As the dune migrates, repeated avalanches build inclined

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.130
layers.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.260
Loess is windblown silt, a different deposit from dune sand.
